                            INSTALLER PROGRAM NOTES

To do:

1. I have seen a mode where the /wg mode compile caused the logo to be 
displayed corrupted. The problem occurred with "logo1.bmp", which was
copied to "logo.bmp", then the loadpict was pointed to that. This "fixed"
the problem. The two files compare identical. A diagnostic placed in
the file found that the picture was being loaded as a 15x16 pixel bitmap,
which tends to indicate it was corrupted (the right answer is 100x375).

2. Make a trial CD ROM with full installation on it. Run that on
various computers.

3. Add Windows product ID to the registration codes (from the WPA key).

4. Add CRC of program (.text) to registration.

5 One idea that might enhance security of the install.dat file is to generate
aribitrary/random data into the file. This can consist of tolkens that indicate
a run of data is to be ignored.

6. An idea to make the install resistant to resetting the clock for time
limited software is to plant a registration key with the current time, 
encyphered, then check that time does not go backwards. Each time the
software comes up, it checks that the time now is past the encyphered
registration time. Because the key is planted when install is done, the
lock can call for reregistration if it finds the key missing or wrong.
This procedure also protects against trying to move the software without
installing it.

